const e=JSON.parse(`{"eco-krach-boursier":{"titre":"Stock market crash","description":"After months of euphoria, the stock market plunges in a single session. Analysts who have sworn for a year that \\"this time it's different\\" find that it was the same as ever. Small shareholders, meanwhile, find their statement.","news":"Crash: stock market collapses in a single session","choix":{"soutien":{"label":"Announce a market support fund","description":"The state buys up shares to stem the panic.","avantage":"Reassures the markets and limits the fall","cout":"Hits the budget and rewards speculators","news":"Crash: state rides to the rescue of the stock market"},"laisser":{"label":"Let the market purge itself","description":"Point out that the stock market goes up and down, and that it is none of the state's business.","avantage":"Deflates the bubble with no public spending","cout":"Brutal losses for savings and activity","news":"Crash: government refuses to intervene"},"epargnants":{"label":"Protect small savers","description":"A targeted scheme for affected households, not for hedge funds.","avantage":"Preserves household confidence","cout":"Budget cost and lukewarm markets","news":"Crash: a safety net for small savers"}}},"eco-bulle-bourse-gonfle":{"titre":"Stock market soars","description":"Indices are breaking record after record, and dinner-party conversation now turns on tech stocks. When your taxi driver gives you investment advice, economists start to sweat.","news":"Stock market: euphoria spreads to dinner tables","choix":{"alerter":{"label":"Warn of the risks","description":"A sober speech on caution and tougher credit rules for speculation.","avantage":"Reduces the risk of a future crash","cout":"Cools the mood and the markets","news":"Stock market: government pulls the handbrake"},"profiter":{"label":"Enjoy the party","description":"Congratulate yourself publicly, as every point on the index is partly your doing.","avantage":"Euphoric mood, popularity and consumption up","cout":"The bubble grows, the fall will be harder","news":"Stock market: those in power applaud the records"},"taxer":{"label":"Tax capital gains","description":"A temporary levy on stock market gains.","avantage":"Immediate tax revenue","cout":"Annoys investors","news":"Stock market: a tax on capital gains"}}},"eco-bulle-immo-eclate":{"titre":"The property bubble bursts","description":"Property prices, which \\"could only go up\\", start to fall. Estate agents promise a \\"simple adjustment\\", while over-indebted households work out that their flat is worth less than their mortgage.","news":"Property: bubble bursts, prices plunge","choix":{"rachat":{"label":"Buy up unsold homes","description":"The state becomes the owner of thousands of homes to prop up prices.","avantage":"Cushions the fall and supports construction","cout":"Costly for the budget","news":"Property: state buys up the unsold homes"},"debiteurs":{"label":"Help indebted households","description":"Supervised renegotiation and deferred repayments.","avantage":"Avoids a wave of repossessions","cout":"Weakens the banks and costs the budget","news":"Property: a support plan for indebted households"},"correction":{"label":"Let the correction run its course","description":"Prices become reasonable again, which is not a misfortune for everyone.","avantage":"More affordable housing in time, budget preserved","cout":"Building sites at a standstill, households in difficulty","news":"Property: government lets the correction take its course"}}},"eco-flambee-bourse":{"titre":"Stock market surge","description":"Driven by better-than-expected company results, the stock market takes off. Bosses talk of \\"solid fundamentals\\", unions of \\"fundamentals for shareholders\\".","news":"Stock market takes off, and so do dividends","choix":{"encourager":{"label":"Encourage productive investment","description":"Incentives so that profits fund the means of production.","avantage":"Investment and growth up","cout":"Tax shortfall","news":"Stock market: incentives to invest profits"},"partage":{"label":"Impose profit-sharing","description":"Employees will get their share of the exceptional dividends.","avantage":"Wages and purchasing power up","cout":"Employers grumble, stock market cooled","news":"Record dividends: employees to get their share"},"rien":{"label":"Do nothing and applaud","description":"When things are going well, you leave well alone.","avantage":"Optimistic mood and delighted markets","cout":"Visible inequalities, bubble swelling","news":"Stock market: government lets it run"}}},"eco-baril-flambe":{"titre":"Oil price soars","description":"Oil prices leap after tensions among the big producers. At the pumps, motorists discover that the green transition was going to come out of their wallets.","news":"Oil: the barrel soars, and so do the pumps","choix":{"bouclier":{"label":"Fuel price shield","description":"The state caps prices at the pump.","avantage":"Immediate relief for households","cout":"High budget bill and oil consumption kept going","news":"Fuel: state caps pump prices"},"cheque":{"label":"Targeted energy voucher","description":"Help only the most exposed.","avantage":"Targeted aid and controlled cost","cout":"Many motorists feel forgotten","news":"Oil: a voucher for the least well off"},"sobriete":{"label":"Energy saving plan","description":"Speed up the shift to rail and renewable energy.","avantage":"Reduces dependence and serves the climate","cout":"Unpopular in the short term","news":"Dear oil: government preaches restraint"}}},"eco-degradation-note":{"titre":"An agency downgrades the rating","description":"The Moody-Blues agency lowers the country's rating, citing a \\"worrying\\" budget trajectory. The Finance Ministry calls it an \\"episode\\"; the markets call it a chance to be paid more.","news":"Moody-Blues downgrades the country's rating","choix":{"economies":{"label":"Credible savings plan","description":"Spending freeze and reforms announced over several years.","avantage":"Reassures lenders and reduces the deficit","cout":"Social spending trimmed, popularity down","news":"Downgrade: the government announces savings"},"contester":{"label":"Challenge the agency","description":"Denounce an ideological judgement and remind everyone of the country's strengths.","avantage":"National pride and public support","cout":"The markets demand a higher rent","news":"Credit rating: the government attacks the agency"},"recettes":{"label":"Raise revenue","description":"An exceptional levy on high earners and big companies.","avantage":"Quick revenue and a sense of fairness","cout":"Entrepreneurs grit their teeth","news":"Downgrade: an exceptional levy"}}},"eco-prime-risque":{"titre":"The risk premium creeps back up","description":"The gap between the country's borrowing rate and that of its more sensible neighbour is widening. Traders call it \\"a spread\\". Taxpayers will soon call it \\"next year's taxes\\".","news":"Spread: the country's risk premium rises","choix":{"signal":{"label":"Send a signal of rigour","description":"Announce a path to reduce the deficit.","avantage":"Brings the risk premium back down","cout":"Austerity and social unrest","news":"Spread: a signal of rigour to reassure"},"banque-centrale":{"label":"Call on the central bank for help","description":"Argue for a bond-buying programme.","avantage":"Eases rates without any savings","cout":"Dependence and a debate over independence","news":"Debt: a nudge to the central bank"},"ignorer":{"label":"Play the event down","description":"\\"No funding problem whatsoever,\\" they say, looking the other way.","avantage":"No immediate sacrifice, mood preserved","cout":"The markets will test the country's resolve","news":"Risk premium: the government plays it down"}}},"eco-adjudication-ratee":{"titre":"Failed debt auction","description":"The Treasury offers its bonds, but investors sulk: the auction is a half-failure, the State having raised barely enough to pay for the coffee. Rates tick up a notch, as one might expect.","news":"Debt: an auction falls flat","choix":{"rendement":{"label":"Offer a better yield","description":"Pay more to win over the lenders.","avantage":"Funding is secured","cout":"Heavier interest costs for years","news":"Debt: the State pays more to borrow"},"epargne":{"label":"Launch a loan from households","description":"A citizens' savings bond with a guaranteed return.","avantage":"National funding and popularity","cout":"Draws savings out of private channels","news":"Debt: a national loan from citizens"},"coupes":{"label":"Cut spending to borrow less","description":"Lower funding needs, hence less dependence on the markets.","avantage":"Eases exposure to investors","cout":"Public services slow down","news":"Debt: budget cuts after a failed auction"}}},"eco-seuil-dette":{"titre":"Debt passes 100% of GDP","description":"The debt counter crosses the symbolic line of a year's worth of wealth produced. Commentators dust off their pendulums, the opposition its clock. Nobody knows who will repay it, everybody knows who will pay.","news":"Debt exceeds 100% of GDP","choix":{"pacte":{"label":"Set a debt ceiling","description":"Write a golden rule into law.","avantage":"Credibility with the markets","cout":"Room for manoeuvre shrinks, the majority grumbles","news":"Debt: a golden rule to curb borrowing"},"croissance":{"label":"Bet on growth","description":"The best way to reduce debt would be to grow GDP.","avantage":"Supports activity and jobs","cout":"Debt keeps climbing","news":"Debt: the government bets on growth"},"restructurer":{"label":"Restructure the debt","description":"Extend maturities and renegotiate the terms.","avantage":"Eases short-term payments","cout":"Image tarnished with investors","news":"Debt: the State renegotiates its maturities"}}},"eco-charge-dette":{"titre":"Debt servicing becomes a major budget item","description":"Debt interest now exceeds the budgets of several ministries combined. The Finance Minister remarks, with questionable wit, that \\"you pay dearly for having borrowed cheaply\\".","news":"Debt: interest devours the budget","choix":{"reformes":{"label":"Undertake structural reforms","description":"Pensions, administration, social spending: the big overhaul.","avantage":"Puts the books right for the long term","cout":"Industrial action and falling popularity","news":"Debt: root-and-branch reforms announced"},"impots":{"label":"Raise taxes","description":"An across-the-board increase to pay the interest.","avantage":"Immediate revenue","cout":"Drag on activity","news":"Debt: tax rises to pay the interest"},"patience":{"label":"Wait for rates to fall","description":"Count on kinder economic conditions.","avantage":"No unpopular measures","cout":"The bill keeps growing in the meantime","news":"Debt: the government waits for better days"}}},"eco-faillite-banque":{"titre":"Collapse of the Continental General Bank","description":"The Continental General Bank, deemed \\"too big to fail\\" not long ago, closes its doors. Depositors queue up, the executives leave with their bonuses, and the Finance Ministry looks for the number of an expert.","news":"The Continental General Bank collapses","choix":{"sauvetage":{"label":"Rescue the bank with public money","description":"Emergency recapitalisation to avoid panic.","avantage":"Avoids contagion and protects depositors","cout":"Public bill and public anger","news":"Bank failure: the State dips into its pocket"},"faillite":{"label":"Let an orderly failure happen","description":"Shareholders and creditors pay, depositors are guaranteed up to a limit.","avantage":"Lower cost to the taxpayer, sets an example","cout":"Shock to credit and to confidence","news":"Bank failure: the State lets the bank fall"},"nationalisation":{"label":"Nationalise temporarily","description":"The State takes control, reassures, and promises to sell it back.","avantage":"Stabilises the system and keeps control","cout":"Debt up, suspicions of collectivism","news":"Bank nationalised: the State takes the helm"}}},"eco-banque-centrale-releve":{"titre":"The central bank raises its rates","description":"To curb inflation, the central bank raises its key interest rates. Borrowers see an injustice, savers good news, the State's treasurer a headache.","news":"The central bank raises its key rates","choix":{"soutenir":{"label":"Publicly back the decision","description":"Hammer home that fighting inflation is the priority.","avantage":"Prices better contained over time, credibility","cout":"Dearer credit, slower activity","news":"Rate rise: the government approves"},"critiquer":{"label":"Criticise the decision","description":"Denounce a brake on growth and jobs.","avantage":"Popularity with borrowers","cout":"Undermines the central bank's independence","news":"Rates: the government pulls a long face"},"compenser":{"label":"Help households with loans","description":"A targeted scheme for variable-rate mortgages.","avantage":"Protects vulnerable borrowers","cout":"Extra spending","news":"Rates rising: a helping hand for borrowers"}}},"eco-banque-centrale-baisse":{"titre":"The central bank cuts its rates","description":"Faced with a slowing economy, the central bank cuts its rates. Credit becomes attractive again, saving less so, and economists argue over whether it is too little or too late.","news":"The central bank cuts its key rates","choix":{"relance":{"label":"Back it with a stimulus plan","description":"Take advantage of lower rates to invest.","avantage":"Boosts activity and jobs","cout":"Debt up","news":"Rates falling: the government stimulates the economy"},"refinancer":{"label":"Refinance the debt cheaply","description":"Extend maturities at the new rates.","avantage":"Lighter debt burden","cout":"Little stimulus for households","news":"Rates falling: the State refinances its debt"},"prudence":{"label":"Warn against inflation","description":"Remind everyone that overly loose monetary policy can prove costly.","avantage":"Credibility on price stability","cout":"Missed chance to support activity","news":"Rates falling: the government plays it cautious"}}},"eco-polemique-banque-centrale":{"titre":"Controversy over the central bank","description":"A report suggests the central bank failed to anticipate inflation. Its leaders swear it is \\"independent\\", which, coming from a banker, sounds like \\"don't ask me to account for myself\\".","news":"Central bank: the controversy grows","choix":{"defendre":{"label":"Defend the institution's independence","description":"Politicians have no business dictating rates.","avantage":"Keeps the markets' confidence","cout":"The public blames you for covering for those responsible","news":"Central bank: the government defends the institution"},"enquete":{"label":"Call for a parliamentary inquiry","description":"Shed full light on the errors of judgement.","avantage":"Transparency and public satisfaction","cout":"Sows doubt about monetary credibility","news":"Central bank: a parliamentary inquiry opened"},"mandat":{"label":"Revise the institution's mandate","description":"Add employment and growth to its objectives.","avantage":"More support for activity in future","cout":"Risk of lasting inflation and confusion","news":"Central bank: the mandate will be reviewed"}}},"eco-credit-crunch":{"titre":"Banks turn off the credit tap","description":"Anxious, the banks tighten their lending conditions. Businesses will tell you they have never had so little to put up as collateral, and the banks that they have never been so cautious.","news":"Credit: the banks tighten the screws","choix":{"garantie":{"label":"Guarantee business loans","description":"The State guarantees a share of new loans.","avantage":"Revives credit and protects jobs","cout":"Potential liability for the budget","news":"Credit: the State guarantees business loans"},"pression":{"label":"Summon the bankers","description":"A meeting at the Palace to remind them of their duties.","avantage":"Political pressure at low cost","cout":"Little effect, and a whiff of interference","news":"Credit: bankers summoned to the Palace"},"regle":{"label":"Relax the prudential rules","description":"Free up capital so that banks lend again.","avantage":"More credit available","cout":"Weakens the banking system","news":"Banks: prudential rules relaxed"}}},"eco-scandale-fiscal":{"titre":"Tax scandal","description":"A press investigation reveals that big corporations pay almost no tax, thanks to tax engineering of remarkable sophistication. Lawyers are admiring, taxpayers less so.","news":"Tax scandal: big groups almost fully exempt","choix":{"reformer":{"label":"Reform corporate taxation","description":"A minimum tax and an end to the most common schemes.","avantage":"Revenue and a sense of justice","cout":"Threats of relocation","news":"Tax scandal: a minimum tax for big groups"},"negocier":{"label":"Negotiate with the companies concerned","description":"An amicable settlement to regularise the sums owed.","avantage":"Modest income without upsetting investors","cout":"Looks like complacency","news":"Tax scandal: the government negotiates"},"minimiser":{"label":"Point out that everything is legal","description":"Just change the law later, preferably even later.","avantage":"Avoids an exodus of capital","cout":"Public anger and an unchanged deficit","news":"Tax scandal: \\"perfectly legal\\""}}},"eco-evasion-fiscale":{"titre":"Tax evasion makes the front page","description":"Leaked documents reveal fortunes sleeping in exotic tax havens. The names mentioned all deny it, with the elegance of people who have good lawyers.","news":"Tax evasion: new revelations","choix":{"traque":{"label":"Step up the hunt for fraudsters","description":"Extra resources for the tax authority.","avantage":"Lasting revenue and fairness","cout":"Upfront investment, tension with investors","news":"Tax evasion: the taxman goes on the offensive"},"amnistie":{"label":"Offer a favourable amnesty","description":"Fraudsters bring their money home with a reduced penalty.","avantage":"Fresh money and capital returning","cout":"Sense of impunity, injustice","news":"Tax evasion: an amnesty at a bargain price"},"international":{"label":"Push for an international agreement","description":"Cooperation between countries to lift banking secrecy.","avantage":"Prestige and lasting effect","cout":"Slow, uncertain results","news":"Tax evasion: the country proposes an international agreement"}}},"eco-niche-fiscale":{"titre":"A tax loophole causes a scandal","description":"A tax loophole created \\"temporarily\\" thirty years ago turns out to cost the State billions, for the benefit of a sector whose lobbying is anything but temporary. Experts call it \\"optimisation\\", the public calls it a \\"gift\\".","news":"Tax loophole: thirty years of \\"temporary\\"","choix":{"supprimer":{"label":"Abolish the loophole","description":"End of the scheme from next year.","avantage":"Immediate savings","cout":"The sector concerned protests, loudly","news":"Tax loophole: the government makes its call"},"reduire":{"label":"Phase it out gradually","description":"A wind-down spread over five years.","avantage":"A compromise that calms the sector","cout":"Modest savings, mixed public opinion","news":"Tax loophole: abolition spread over five years"},"maintenir":{"label":"Keep it, to be safe","description":"A loophole also means jobs, so they say.","avantage":"Peace with the sector and jobs preserved","cout":"Lost revenue, accusations of favouritism","news":"Tax loophole: the government keeps it"}}},"eco-recettes-record":{"titre":"Record tax revenue","description":"Thanks to livelier activity than expected, the State's coffers are filling faster than anticipated. The Finance Ministry talks of a \\"windfall\\", the spendthrift ministers of \\"their windfall\\".","news":"Tax revenue: an unexpected bonanza","choix":{"desendetter":{"label":"Reduce the deficit","description":"Put the entire surplus towards paying down debt.","avantage":"Debt down, market confidence","cout":"No benefit for citizens","news":"Record revenue: the State pays down debt"},"baisse-impots":{"label":"Cut taxes","description":"Give citizens back what belongs to them, or nearly.","avantage":"Purchasing power and popularity","cout":"Reduced future revenue, risk of overheating","news":"Record revenue: a tax cut announced"},"investir":{"label":"Invest in infrastructure","description":"Hospitals, schools, networks: catching up on the backlog.","avantage":"Future growth and public services","cout":"Immediate cost, slow benefits","news":"Record revenue: the State invests"}}},"eco-affaire-financiere":{"titre":"Financial affair at the top","description":"An adviser close to the government is accused of playing the stock market with confidential information. He explains that he \\"was simply lucky\\". Luck, apparently, is a very well-paid skill.","news":"Insider trading: someone close to power in the frame","choix":{"demission":{"label":"Demand his immediate resignation","description":"Cut it short and let the courts do their work.","avantage":"Saves the government's image","cout":"Weakens the majority and suggests an admission of guilt","news":"Insider trading: the adviser sacrificed"},"defendre":{"label":"Defend the adviser","description":"The presumption of innocence, we are reminded, applies to everyone.","avantage":"Support from the majority","cout":"Hostile public opinion","news":"Insider trading: the Palace defends its adviser"},"loi":{"label":"Announce a transparency law","description":"A register of interests and tougher checks.","avantage":"A structural response, an image of rigour","cout":"Embarrasses the majority and business circles","news":"Insider trading: a transparency law announced"}}},"eco-fonds-pension":{"titre":"The pension fund lost the money","description":"A major pension fund invested millions of employees' pensions in \\"innovative\\" products that nobody could explain. It has just lost a quarter of its value, in an equally innovative fashion.","news":"Pensions: a pension fund loses a quarter of its assets","choix":{"garantir":{"label":"Guarantee pensions","description":"The State covers the losses for pensioners.","avantage":"Protects pensioners, calms the country","cout":"Hefty bill for the budget","news":"Pension fund: the State guarantees pensions"},"responsables":{"label":"Prosecute the managers","description":"An investigation and exemplary penalties.","avantage":"Public satisfaction and deterrence","cout":"No immediate repayment, markets cooled","news":"Pension fund: prosecutions announced"},"regle":{"label":"Regulate funds more strictly","description":"Cap risky products in portfolios.","avantage":"Prevents a future disaster","cout":"Managers cry stifling","news":"Pension fund: tougher regulation"}}},"eco-cour-des-comptes":{"titre":"Court of Auditors report","description":"The Court of Auditors publishes a damning report on the management of several administrations. It recommends \\"spending better\\", advice it has repeated pretty much every year since it was founded.","news":"Court of Auditors: a damning report","choix":{"appliquer":{"label":"Apply the recommendations","description":"Reform spending, eliminate duplication.","avantage":"Savings and gain in credibility","cout":"Tension with the civil service","news":"Court of Auditors: the government will follow its advice"},"contester":{"label":"Dispute the figures","description":"Point out that the Court does not always see the nuances.","avantage":"Protects the administration and the majority","cout":"Looks like denial","news":"Court of Auditors: the government disputes the findings"},"commission":{"label":"Set up a review commission","description":"A commission will study the report, then study itself.","avantage":"Buys time, avoids conflict","cout":"Few results and a whiff of burial","news":"Court of Auditors: a commission to study the report"}}},"eco-subventions-fantomes":{"titre":"The ghost subsidies","description":"An audit reveals that public subsidies funded companies that do not exist, or more precisely that exist only on paper, on the third floor of a building with no lift. The money, however, did exist.","news":"Public subsidies: ghost companies pocket millions","choix":{"audit":{"label":"Launch a general audit of aid","description":"Check each scheme, one by one.","avantage":"Money recovered, aid cleaned up","cout":"Delays for genuine businesses","news":"Subsidies: a general audit of public aid"},"poursuites":{"label":"Prosecute the fraudsters","description":"Court proceedings and seizures.","avantage":"Justice and deterrence","cout":"Slow courts, little short-term revenue","news":"Ghost subsidies: fraudsters prosecuted"},"discretion":{"label":"Quietly hush up the affair","description":"A few corrections to the accounts, a terse press release.","avantage":"Avoids scandal and paralysis","cout":"Risk of discovery and lasting distrust","news":"Ghost subsidies: the affair fizzles out"}}},"eco-bonus-banquiers":{"titre":"The bankers' bonuses","description":"While the country grits its teeth, a major bank pays record bonuses to its market traders. The chief executive insists they are \\"performance bonuses\\", which the bank's customers find hard to believe when reading their account fees.","news":"Bankers' bonuses: anger grows","choix":{"plafonner":{"label":"Cap bonuses by law","description":"A ceiling tied to fixed salary and the bank's results.","avantage":"Popular response and fairness","cout":"Banks threaten to leave and the financial centre worries","news":"Bank bonuses: the law sets a cap"},"taxe":{"label":"Tax exceptional bonuses","description":"A levy on the highest pay.","avantage":"Immediate revenue","cout":"Likely workarounds, grumbling from those affected","news":"Bank bonuses: an exceptional tax"},"laisser":{"label":"Let the banks regulate themselves","description":"They promise to \\"reflect on their practices\\".","avantage":"No conflict with the financial centre","cout":"Government image tarnished with households","news":"Bank bonuses: the government trusts the banks"}}},"eco-hausse-petrole":{"titre":"The barrel soars","description":"Producer countries tighten the taps and the price of a barrel hits record highs. At petrol stations, queues lengthen to watch the displayed price change live. An adviser suggests \\"anticipating the trend\\", without saying in which direction.","news":"Oil: the barrel soars, and so do the pumps","choix":{"bouclier-carburant":{"label":"Fuel discount","description":"A discount at the pump funded by the budget.","avantage":"Purchasing power protected, motorists soothed","cout":"Public bill and an anti-green signal","news":"Fuel: a discount at the pump"},"sobriete-mobilite":{"label":"Sobriety plan and transport","description":"Encourage car-sharing and public transport.","avantage":"Spares both the environment and the budget","cout":"Motorists grumble, activity slows","news":"Fuel: the government calls on drivers to ease off"},"reserves":{"label":"Tap into strategic reserves","description":"Release stock to calm the market.","avantage":"Barrel price curbed, security of supply on display","cout":"Reserves depleted and public spending","news":"Oil: strategic reserves put on the market"}}},"eco-crise-energie-industrie":{"titre":"Factory energy bills","description":"Industrialists dependent on energy imports see their bills explode and threaten to switch off the furnaces. Employers demand aid, unions demand guarantees, and everyone demands heating.","news":"Industry: the energy bill makes factories wobble","choix":{"aide-industrie":{"label":"Aid for energy-hungry industries","description":"Subsidise part of the energy bill.","avantage":"Factories saved, jobs preserved","cout":"High spending, windfall for some","news":"Energy: a cheque for the big factories"},"delestage":{"label":"Scheduled load shedding","description":"Cut off power to sites at peak hours.","avantage":"Budget and grid protected, green signal sent","cout":"Lost output and furious employers","news":"Energy: factories idled at peak hours"},"contrats-long-terme":{"label":"Long-term supply contracts","description":"Negotiate with foreign suppliers.","avantage":"Price stability in the medium term","cout":"Diplomatic debt and immediate cost","news":"Energy: new contracts signed abroad"}}},"eco-baisse-prix-petrole":{"titre":"The barrel deflates","description":"The oil price collapses, to the great relief of motorists and the great dismay of producer countries. The Finance Ministry dreams of taxes, the Ecology Ministry dreams of fewer cars, and everyone dreams of being right.","news":"Oil: barrel at a knockdown price","choix":{"laisser-profiter":{"label":"Let prices fall","description":"Leave fuel taxation alone.","avantage":"Purchasing power and popularity up","cout":"Lower revenue, emissions rebound","news":"Fuel: the pumps finally smile"},"taxer":{"label":"Raise the fuel tax","description":"Capture part of the windfall for the budget.","avantage":"Net revenue and a green signal","cout":"Motorists' anger","news":"Fuel: the State takes its cut of the fall"},"fonds-transition":{"label":"Energy transition fund","description":"Channel the windfall towards renewables.","avantage":"Investment in the future and less dependence","cout":"Nothing for households right now","news":"Energy: the falling barrel funds the transition"}}},"eco-penurie-carburant":{"titre":"Fuel shortage","description":"Petrol stations are closing for lack of deliveries and motorists are filling jerrycans as if before a siege. Social media overflows with supply-chain experts, each more assertive than the last.","news":"Shortage: dry stations, frayed nerves","choix":{"rationnement":{"label":"Temporary rationing","description":"Limit volumes per vehicle.","avantage":"Order and fairness, the shortage calms down","cout":"Discontent and slowed activity","news":"Fuel: rationing introduced"},"importation-urgence":{"label":"Emergency imports","description":"Buy at top price on the world market.","avantage":"Stations fill up quickly","cout":"Budget bled dry and prices up","news":"Fuel: cargoes bought in a hurry"},"laisser-prix":{"label":"Let prices adjust","description":"Count on the market to rebalance.","avantage":"Budget spared, supply returns","cout":"Low-income households sacrificed","news":"Fuel: the market decides, households pay"}}},"eco-inflation-emballement":{"titre":"Inflation runs away","description":"Prices are climbing faster than wages and the weekly shop is becoming a combat sport. Commentators talk of a “spiral”, households of “the supermarket”, and the central bank of “vigilance”, which reassures nobody.","news":"Inflation: prices soar, households fall behind","choix":{"hausse-taux":{"label":"Back the rate rise","description":"Support a firm monetary policy.","avantage":"Inflation curbed, credibility strengthened","cout":"Dearer credit, slower activity","news":"Inflation: the central bank tightens the screw"},"bouclier-prix":{"label":"Anti-inflation shield","description":"Cap certain prices and hand out cheques.","avantage":"Purchasing power protected in the short term","cout":"Budget overshoot","news":"Inflation: capped prices on the shelves"},"indexation":{"label":"Index wages","description":"Encourage pay rises.","avantage":"Households reassured, social cohesion","cout":"Risk of a spiral and costs for businesses","news":"Inflation: wages chase prices"}}},"eco-deflation-menace":{"titre":"The spectre of deflation","description":"Prices are stagnating, even falling, and consumers are waiting for sales that never end. Businesses delay investing, households delay buying, and everyone waits for someone else to go first.","news":"Prices flat: deflation looms","choix":{"relance-budget":{"label":"Fiscal stimulus","description":"Inject public money into the economy.","avantage":"Demand and jobs boosted","cout":"Deficit widened","news":"Stimulus: the State reopens the floodgates"},"baisse-taux":{"label":"Push for lower rates","description":"Get cheaper credit.","avantage":"Investment and property revived","cout":"Risk of a bubble, savers unhappy","news":"Deflation: credit gets cheaper"},"patience":{"label":"Rush nothing","description":"Trust in spontaneous adjustment.","avantage":"Healthy public finances","cout":"Sluggish growth, impatient voters","news":"Deflation: the government waits, and so do prices"}}},"eco-bon-chiffre-chomage":{"titre":"Unemployment at a low","description":"The statistics institute announces a historically low unemployment rate. The opposition suspects the figures, the majority sees a miracle, and economists timidly point out that firms are struggling to recruit.","news":"Jobs: unemployment at a low","choix":{"fete":{"label":"Savour the success","description":"Make this figure the heart of the communication.","avantage":"Popularity and parliamentary support","cout":"Hidden insecurity, cohesion neglected","news":"Jobs: the government celebrates its record"},"formation":{"label":"Training plan","description":"Steer people towards shortage occupations.","avantage":"Better-equipped workers, a sturdier economy","cout":"Immediate spending","news":"Jobs: a plan for shortage occupations"},"reforme-aides":{"label":"Tighten unemployment benefits","description":"Take advantage of the economic climate to save money.","avantage":"Savings and an incentive to return to work","cout":"The most vulnerable made more fragile","news":"Jobs: benefit rules toughened"}}},"eco-recession":{"titre":"Recession sets in","description":"Gross domestic product shrinks for the second quarter running and the word “recession” officially enters everyday vocabulary. Press conferences become exercises in style: officials speak of a “slight slowdown”.","news":"Recession: the economy shrinks","choix":{"relance":{"label":"Massive stimulus plan","description":"Invest in infrastructure and consumption.","avantage":"Activity and jobs supported","cout":"Debt increased","news":"Recession: a stimulus plan on credit"},"austerite":{"label":"Budget discipline","description":"Cut spending to reassure the markets.","avantage":"Credibility and healthier finances","cout":"Deeper recession, social anger","news":"Recession: the government tightens the screw"},"soutien-entreprises":{"label":"Support for businesses","description":"Cut payroll charges and guarantee credit.","avantage":"Jobs preserved, investment revived","cout":"No helping hand for households","news":"Recession: an umbrella for businesses"}}},"eco-relance-spontanee":{"titre":"An unexpected rebound","description":"Against all forecasts, consumption is picking up and order books are filling. Every minister claims paternity of the recovery, economists talk of “cyclical factors”, and nobody listens to them.","news":"Rebound: growth surprises everyone","choix":{"accompagner":{"label":"Invest in the momentum","description":"Fund infrastructure and innovation.","avantage":"Prolonged recovery, greater competitiveness","cout":"Budget put under strain","news":"Recovery: the State bets on momentum"},"assainir":{"label":"Seize the chance to pay down debt","description":"Save the extra revenue.","avantage":"Debt eased, markets reassured","cout":"Households denied the dividends of recovery","news":"Recovery: the revenue goes on repayments"},"baisse-impots":{"label":"Tax cuts","description":"Redistribute part of the fruits of growth.","avantage":"Purchasing power and popularity","cout":"Revenue down, risk of overheating","news":"Recovery: tax cuts for everyone"}}},"eco-gains-productivite":{"titre":"Productivity leap","description":"A report shows that productivity is finally rising, thanks to machines, software and fewer meetings. Employees want their slice of the cake, and so do shareholders, and the cake is not growing at that rate.","news":"Productivity: work pays more, but for whom?","choix":{"partager":{"label":"Share the gains","description":"Encourage pay rises.","avantage":"Purchasing power and cohesion","cout":"Margins squeezed, businesses cautious","news":"Productivity: employees demand their share"},"compet":{"label":"Bet on competitiveness","description":"Let businesses reinvest.","avantage":"Growth and exports stimulated","cout":"Inequality and social grumbling","news":"Productivity: businesses keep control"},"taxer-gains":{"label":"Tax windfall profits","description":"Capture part of the gains for the community.","avantage":"Public revenue up","cout":"Investment climate damaged","news":"Productivity: a much-criticised tax on gains"}}},"eco-boom-numerique":{"titre":"The digital sector is buzzing","description":"The country's start-ups are raising funds at a speed that makes bankers nervous and accountants romantic. Campuses are opening everywhere, “unicorns” are being born, and every meeting begins with “disruption”.","news":"Digital: the tech sector runs wild","choix":{"zone-franche":{"label":"Technology free zone","description":"Tax breaks to attract talent and capital.","avantage":"Economy and skilled jobs","cout":"Lost revenue and inequality between regions","news":"Digital: a free zone for start-ups"},"regulation":{"label":"Regulate the sector","description":"Data protection and competition rules.","avantage":"Digital security and fairness","cout":"Brake on momentum, investors cooled","news":"Digital: a regulatory framework to calm things down"},"souverain":{"label":"Digital sovereign fund","description":"The State takes stakes in the gems.","avantage":"Strategic control and future returns","cout":"Public money at risk","news":"Digital: the State as shareholder of its gems"}}},"eco-crise-agricole":{"titre":"The fields are angry","description":"Prices down, costs up, bad weather: farmers are coming into town with their tractors, which traffic does not much appreciate. The public is supportive, as long as the blockade is not outside their own door.","news":"Farmers: tractors in town","choix":{"aides-urgence":{"label":"Emergency aid","description":"An immediate support fund.","avantage":"Anger soothed, rural cohesion","cout":"Spending without deep reform","news":"Agriculture: an emergency fund released"},"transition-agro":{"label":"Agroecological transition","description":"Support the move to new practices.","avantage":"Ecology and the sector's future","cout":"Painful transition, immediate grumbling","news":"Agriculture: the State proposes a green turn"},"prix-planchers":{"label":"Price floors","description":"Guarantee a minimum price.","avantage":"Stable incomes for producers","cout":"Dearer shopping for everyone","news":"Agriculture: price floors introduced"}}},"eco-saison-touristique-record":{"titre":"Record tourist season","description":"Beaches, museums and inns are all full, and locals are discovering that their town centre has turned into a postcard set. Hoteliers smile, residents sigh, and the seagulls are indifferent.","news":"Tourism: a record-breaking season","choix":{"investir-tourisme":{"label":"Invest in capacity","description":"Hotels, transport, visitor sites.","avantage":"Lasting revenue and jobs","cout":"Overcrowding and a heavier footprint","news":"Tourism: investment for the influx"},"taxe-sejour":{"label":"Stronger tourist tax","description":"Make visitors contribute.","avantage":"Revenue and regulation of visitor flows","cout":"Visitors put off","news":"Tourism: a tax for visitors"},"quotas":{"label":"Quotas on fragile sites","description":"Limit access to preserve heritage.","avantage":"Sites protected, residents relieved","cout":"Lost earnings for shopkeepers","news":"Tourism: quotas at the gates of the sites"}}},"eco-desindustrialisation":{"titre":"The factories go dark","description":"A report confirms that industry is losing sites, jobs and know-how every quarter. The old industrial heartlands increasingly resemble museums, with fewer visitors.","news":"Industry: the decline is confirmed","choix":{"reindustrialisation":{"label":"Reindustrialisation plan","description":"Subsidies and land to bring production back home.","avantage":"Jobs and sovereignty regained","cout":"High cost, slow results","news":"Industry: a grand relocalisation plan"},"reconversion-sites":{"label":"Regional reconversion","description":"Support the shift to services and digital.","avantage":"Local rebound and cohesion","cout":"Industry keeps fading away","news":"Industry: regions turned towards the future"},"laisser-marche":{"label":"Laissez-faire","description":"Rely on comparative advantage.","avantage":"Budget preserved, consistent free-market message","cout":"Local unemployment and anger","news":"Industry: the State leaves it to the market"}}},"eco-fleuron-industriel":{"titre":"A coveted jewel","description":"The country's industrial champion, proud of its patents and its workers, is the target of a foreign takeover bid. Shareholders are delighted, unions worried, and the Palace is already talking about “sovereignty”.","news":"Industry: the national flagship in a foreign fund's sights","choix":{"bloquer":{"label":"Block the takeover","description":"Veto it in the name of the national interest.","avantage":"Jobs and know-how protected","cout":"Image damaged with investors","news":"Industry: the State opposes the takeover"},"accepter":{"label":"Welcome the investor","description":"Let it happen in return for job guarantees.","avantage":"Capital and international openness","cout":"Loss of control, social fears","news":"Industry: the flagship passes under a foreign flag"},"action-or":{"label":"State golden share","description":"Take a stake with a right of veto.","avantage":"Strategic control retained","cout":"Cost to the budget","news":"Industry: the State takes a golden share"}}},"eco-chute-monnaie":{"titre":"The currency slides","description":"The national currency is losing ground against the major currencies, and foreign tourists suddenly feel very rich. Importers, for their part, count on their fingers, then on their colleagues' fingers.","news":"Exchange rate: the currency plunges","choix":{"hausse-taux-change":{"label":"Raise rates","description":"Defend the currency with higher rates.","avantage":"Currency stabilised, confidence restored","cout":"Dearer credit, growth slowed","news":"Exchange rate: the central bank defends the currency"},"laisser-deriver":{"label":"Let the currency slide","description":"Benefit from a more competitive currency.","avantage":"Exports boosted","cout":"Dearer imports, purchasing power eroded","news":"Exchange rate: a weak currency, exports in good shape"},"reserves-change":{"label":"Dip into foreign exchange reserves","description":"Intervene on the markets.","avantage":"Immediate relief","cout":"Reserves depleted, temporary effect","news":"Exchange rate: massive intervention on the markets"}}},"eco-deficit-commercial":{"titre":"Abysmal trade deficit","description":"The country imports far more than it exports, prompting heated debates about “made here”. Consumers, for their part, keep buying goods made elsewhere, out of sheer consistency.","news":"Foreign trade: the deficit widens","choix":{"made-in":{"label":"“Buy local” campaign","description":"Encourage domestic consumption.","avantage":"Local production stimulated, pride regained","cout":"Higher prices, tension with partners","news":"Trade: everyone behind made-in-local"},"subventions-export":{"label":"Help exporters","description":"Export credit and insurance.","avantage":"Foreign sales supported","cout":"Budget cost","news":"Trade: a helping hand for exporters"},"accepter-deficit":{"label":"Accept the deficit","description":"Cheap imports support purchasing power.","avantage":"Low prices for households","cout":"Dependence and external fragility","news":"Trade: is the deficit a necessary evil?"}}},"eco-droits-de-douane":{"titre":"Tariff war","description":"A major trading partner abruptly raises its tariffs on our products, citing a “necessary rebalancing”. Exporters call the Palace, which promises to call back after the meeting.","news":"Trade: new taxes on our products","choix":{"riposter":{"label":"Retaliate with taxes","description":"Apply equivalent tariffs.","avantage":"Firmness and popularity","cout":"Imported prices up, relations strained","news":"Customs: the country hits back in turn"},"negocier":{"label":"Negotiate a compromise","description":"Talk to limit the damage.","avantage":"Diplomatic image preserved","cout":"Concessions criticised, partial effect","news":"Customs: negotiations begin"},"compenser":{"label":"Compensate the affected sectors","description":"Targeted aid for exporters.","avantage":"Jobs preserved","cout":"Public bill","news":"Customs: the State compensates exporters"}}},"eco-accord-commercial":{"titre":"Free trade agreement","description":"A vast trade agreement with distant partners is on the table. Exporters applaud, protected producers choke, and everyone cites the same study, which says different things depending on the page.","news":"Trade: a free trade agreement in sight","choix":{"signer":{"label":"Sign without reservation","description":"Open up the markets.","avantage":"Exports and international openness","cout":"Fragile sectors exposed","news":"Trade: the agreement is signed"},"signer-clauses":{"label":"Sign with safeguard clauses","description":"Negotiate social and environmental protections.","avantage":"Acceptable balance, image under control","cout":"Reduced trade gain, costly negotiation","news":"Trade: an agreement with safeguards"},"refuser":{"label":"Reject the agreement","description":"Protect sensitive sectors.","avantage":"Producers reassured, sovereignty on display","cout":"Opportunities lost, closed-off image","news":"Trade: the country says no to the agreement"}}},"eco-fuite-capitaux":{"titre":"Capital flight","description":"Foreign investors are pulling out their chips faster than they put them in, and rumours travel faster than bank transfers. One analyst speaks of a “loss of confidence”; another, more bluntly, of “panic”.","news":"Markets: capital leaves the country","choix":{"controle-capitaux":{"label":"Capital controls","description":"Limit outflows of money.","avantage":"Haemorrhage stopped","cout":"International image dented","news":"Markets: limits on capital movements"},"taux-haut":{"label":"Raise rates and reassure","description":"Make the country more attractive.","avantage":"Confidence restored","cout":"Dearer credit, growth slowed","news":"Markets: higher rates to hold on to capital"},"garanties-fiscales":{"label":"Tax guarantees for investors","description":"Promise stability and perks.","avantage":"Capital retained or brought home","cout":"Controversial tax gift","news":"Markets: perks for investors"}}},"eco-greve-transports":{"titre":"Transport strike","description":"Trains at a standstill, metros closed, airports deserted: the unions make their voices heard and commuters mostly hear silence. Editorialists denounce hostage-taking, then take their bikes.","news":"Strike: transport at a standstill","choix":{"negocier-greve":{"label":"Open negotiations","description":"Grant pay concessions.","avantage":"Calm returns, cohesion","cout":"Budget cost, awkward precedent","news":"Strike: the unions win negotiations"},"service-minimum":{"label":"Impose a minimum service","description":"Requisition staff and keep a service running.","avantage":"Activity maintained, authority displayed","cout":"Social tension heightened","news":"Strike: a minimum service imposed"},"attendre":{"label":"Let it fester","description":"Wait for the movement to run out of steam.","avantage":"Budget preserved, no concessions","cout":"Activity paralysed, grumbling","news":"Strike: the government waits, and so do commuters"}}},"eco-hausse-smic":{"titre":"Minimum wage rise demanded","description":"Unions and associations demand a sharp rise in the minimum wage, while employers and chambers of commerce predict the end of the world. Sector-level pay talks, meanwhile, bog down in the corridors with the coffee cups.","news":"Wages: the minimum wage rise at the heart of the debate","choix":{"hausse-forte":{"label":"Substantial rise in the minimum wage","description":"Raise it significantly.","avantage":"Purchasing power of the lowest earners","cout":"Costs for businesses, risk of inflation","news":"Wages: minimum wage raised"},"hausse-modeste":{"label":"Moderate rise and relief measures","description":"Offset it with cuts in payroll charges.","avantage":"Acceptable compromise","cout":"Both sides dissatisfied","news":"Wages: a compromise that pleases no one"},"gel":{"label":"Minimum wage freeze","description":"Protect competitiveness.","avantage":"Businesses relieved, budget protected","cout":"Social anger, purchasing power in decline","news":"Wages: minimum wage stays frozen"}}},"eco-plan-social":{"titre":"Mass redundancy plan","description":"A major company announces thousands of job cuts to \\"regain competitiveness\\". The employees learn the news from a press release, the management from its quarterly results.","news":"Jobs: redundancy plan hits hard","choix":{"encadrer":{"label":"Regulate the redundancy plan","description":"Require redeployment and severance pay.","avantage":"Workers protected, social climate calmed","cout":"Businesses unhappy, restructuring costs","news":"Jobs: the State imposes safeguards for workers"},"aide-entreprise":{"label":"Aid to the company in exchange for keeping jobs","description":"Subsidise to save jobs.","avantage":"Jobs partly saved","cout":"Public money committed, uncertain results","news":"Jobs: aid in exchange for commitments"},"laisser-faire-social":{"label":"Laissez-faire","description":"Respect freedom of enterprise.","avantage":"Competitiveness preserved, budget intact","cout":"Local unemployment, damaged image","news":"Jobs: the redundancy plan runs its course"}}},"eco-pandemie-economie":{"titre":"Epidemic wave","description":"A new epidemic brings the country to a standstill: offices closed, restaurants empty, pharmacies stormed. Every expert has an opinion, sometimes two, often contradictory, and all of them are on television.","news":"Epidemic: the economy in a mask","choix":{"confinement":{"label":"Strict restrictions","description":"Limit travel and gatherings.","avantage":"Public health protected","cout":"Activity devastated, services at a standstill","news":"Epidemic: the country goes into lockdown"},"soutien-large":{"label":"Massive support for the economy","description":"Furlough schemes, guaranteed loans.","avantage":"Jobs and businesses preserved","cout":"Debt on the rise","news":"Epidemic: a large-scale safety net"},"laisser-circuler":{"label":"Minimal measures","description":"Keep activity going as much as possible.","avantage":"Economy less affected","cout":"Health risk, anger among healthcare workers","news":"Epidemic: the government bets on activity"}}}}`),t={t01:{texte:"Unemployment falls, statisticians demand a recount as a precaution"},t02:{texte:"Growth looking good: economists no longer know what to forecast, so they forecast what comes next"},t03:{texte:'The stock market soars, the pub pundits suddenly discover "shares"'},t04:{texte:"Inflation under control: the price of a baguette holds steady, and the baker is surprised herself"},t05:{texte:"Businesses regain their spirits and demand, in return, new reasons to complain",si:[{var:"confianceEntreprises"}]},t06:{texte:"Households are spending again: café terraces are full on a Tuesday morning",si:[{var:"confianceMenages"}]},t07:{texte:"Trade surplus: the country sells more than it buys, and customs officers smile for the first time",si:[{var:"balanceCommerciale"}]},t08:{texte:'The debt rating is upgraded: agencies praise "an almost suspicious discipline"'},t09:{texte:"The country borrows at low rates: lenders queue up, some with croissants",si:[{var:"tauxEmprunt"}]},t10:{texte:'The digital sector is hiring in droves; the head office coffee machine is judged "inadequate"'},t11:{texte:"Record tourist season: museums report more visitors than paintings"},t12:{texte:"Bumper harvests: farmers have yet to find anything to complain about, investigation ongoing"},t13:{texte:"Industrial output picks up: a chimney smoked again yesterday, and the public applauds"},t14:{texte:"The price of a barrel collapses, drivers fill up their tanks with an air of revenge"},t15:{texte:"Debt falls relative to national wealth; the Finance Ministry asks to sit down",si:[{var:"detteRatio"}]},t16:{texte:'Public finances are balanced: a rare event, immediately classified as a "natural phenomenon"'},t17:{texte:"The national currency strengthens: foreign tourists grumble, importers rejoice",si:[{var:"changeIndice"}]},t18:{texte:"Wages rise faster than prices; a trade unionist asks for the calculator to be checked"},t19:{texte:"The energy sector posts solid profits; bills, meanwhile, remain mysteriously steep"},t20:{texte:"Foreign investment up: developers suddenly discover the charm of our provinces",si:[{var:"confianceEntreprises"}]},t21:{texte:"Unemployment climbs: the country now has more expert opinions than job vacancies"},t22:{texte:"Recession confirmed: the country produces less than before, but talks about it more"},t23:{texte:"Inflation runs wild: a coffee on a terrace now costs more than a philosophy lecture"},t24:{texte:"Stock market crash: brokers discover the virtues of gardening and meditation"},t25:{texte:"The cost of debt rises: the Finance Ministry advises no longer opening letters from the bank",si:[{var:"tauxEmprunt"}]},t26:{texte:`The country's rating is downgraded: agencies cite "a hard-to-read trajectory"`},t27:{texte:"Default risk: creditors already ask whether there is a plan B, and a plan C for plan B",si:[{var:"risqueDefaut"}]},t28:{texte:"Oil prices soar: drivers seriously consider walking and poetry"},t29:{texte:"Record trade deficit: we even import received wisdom, laments a columnist",si:[{var:"balanceCommerciale"}]},t30:{texte:"Households close their purses: shopkeepers watch for customers the way one watches for a storm",si:[{var:"confianceMenages"}]},t31:{texte:"Business leaders are in the doldrums: the doldrums, for their part, are out of stock",si:[{var:"confianceEntreprises"}]},t32:{texte:"Debt hits a peak: the Finance Ministry's calculators ask for days off",si:[{var:"detteRatio"}]},t33:{texte:"Public deficit out of control: the figures are so red that the printer is running out of ink"},t34:{texte:"The currency plunges, holidays abroad become a rich person's sport",si:[{var:"changeIndice"}]},t35:{texte:"Property bubble: a fifteen-square-metre studio is now priced like a castle",si:[{var:"bulleImmo"}]},t36:{texte:'Stock market bubble: one analyst warns, three others reply "no, look at the charts"',si:[{var:"bulleBourse"}]},t37:{texte:"Factories close one after another: the last worker switches off the light, then the debate"},t38:{texte:"Drought: farmers scan the sky and a minister, with no more results on either side"},t39:{texte:"Tourists shun the country: unsold postcards now form a landscape of their own"},t40:{texte:"Energy dependence: a neighbour's power cut is enough to black out half the country",si:[{var:"dependanceEnergie"}]},t41:{texte:"Stagflation: prices up, activity down, economists look for a more polite adjective"},t42:{texte:"Property in free fall: estate agents now offer viewings with tea and condolences"},t43:{texte:"Purchasing power in decline: the shopping basket is searched twice by the shopper herself",si:[null,{var:"confianceMenages"}]},t44:{texte:"The digital sector coughs: unicorns turn into ponies, then into carthorses"},t45:{texte:"Energy prices climb: grandmothers talk about wearing gloves indoors again, with pride"},t46:{texte:'The Grand Institute of Forecasting announces that the economy will go "either better or worse"'},t47:{texte:'An expert calls the situation "mixed", which spares him, as usual, from picking a side'},t48:{texte:"The key interest rate is unchanged: the central bank stresses that it is watching, very closely"},t49:{texte:"Economists divided on the recovery: rare consensus that nobody agrees on anything"},t50:{texte:"The Finance Ministry publishes a 400-page report; the summary runs to three, one of them blank"},t51:{texte:"Economic outlook: the country wavers between caution and optimism, so it has chosen cautious optimism"},t52:{texte:"Borrowing rates rise: households discover that patience has a rate too",si:[{var:"tauxDirecteur"}]},t53:{texte:"The central bank cuts its rates: borrowers applaud, savers sigh politely",si:[{var:"tauxDirecteur"}]},t54:{texte:'The country enters its umpteenth economic "turning point", according to the latest editorial'},t55:{texte:"A poll reveals that 70% of citizens do not understand GDP, and neither do the other 30%"},t56:{texte:"Oil prices fluctuate: forecasters see a sign in it; the barrel has made no statement"},t57:{texte:"The stock market stagnates: traders say it is very interesting and check the time"},t58:{texte:"Employment figures will be published tomorrow; the commentary is already written"},t59:{texte:'The public deficit widens slightly: the Finance Ministry speaks of "budgetary breathing room"'},t60:{texte:"Quiet property market: buyers and sellers eye each other, waiting for the other to give in"}},a={c01:{nom:"Aurélien Vasseur-Maldant",fonction:'liberal columnist at "The Market Daily"',texte:'With a debt like this, every euro borrowed is a euro stolen from our grandchildren. It is high time the presidency discovered the word "savings". It exists. I have seen it.',si:[{var:"detteRatio"}]},c02:{nom:"Solange Brétignolle",fonction:`columnist at "The People's Tribune"`,texte:"Unemployment is finally falling and one dares to say the President's policy has something to do with it. The purists will grumble, but this morning, people have jobs. That is already something."},c03:{nom:"Gaspard Lemoult",fonction:'star analyst at the channel "Capital Direct"',texte:'Prices are flying away faster than a pigeon in front of a cat. Purchasing power is melting and the presidency talks to us about "economic conditions". My shopping trolley talks about despair.'},c04:{nom:"Honorine Castellane-Roux",fonction:`editor-in-chief of "The Savers' Courier"`,texte:"The stock market is prancing and everyone thinks they are a financial genius. Let me remind you that bubbles always looked solid, right up to the second they no longer were. A little caution is called for.",si:[{var:"bulleBourse"}]},c05:{nom:"Évariste Podensac",fonction:'in-house economist at "The Industry Journal"',texte:"We let our factories die in the hope that an app would come along to replace them. Result: no more factories, and the app crashes. A little industrial policy would be welcome."},c06:{nom:"Mathilde Granjon",fonction:'columnist at "The Markets Echo"',texte:"Solid growth, contained inflation, confidence restored: I have been looking for the flaw since this morning and cannot find it. So I shall worry on principle, but with goodwill."},c07:{nom:"Théophile Ancelin",fonction:'columnist at "The Social Morning"',texte:"Recession, unemployment, and a government assuring us that all is well. At this stage, it is no longer optimism, it is contemporary art. The queues at the counter, for their part, are very real."},c08:{nom:"Perrine Lavaud-Sorel",fonction:'head of the economics desk at "The Taxpayer Gazette"',texte:"The deficit widens, the State borrows and interest eats the budget. Soon we will be working solely to repay the loan. A fine investment, it must be said."},c09:{nom:"Ambroise Tellier",fonction:'columnist at "The Rating Agencies Journal"',texte:"The country's rating is slipping and borrowing rates are climbing: the market has spoken, it has even raised its voice. It is for the presidency to listen before the bill is written in capital letters.",si:[null,{var:"tauxEmprunt"}]},c10:{nom:"Clémence Dufaure-Lenoir",fonction:'guest economist on "Radio Perspectives"',texte:"For once, public finances can breathe. Debt down, deficit contained, low rates: one could almost speak of management. The word is unusual enough to be underlined.",si:[{var:"detteRatio"}]},c11:{nom:"Barnabé Quéméner",fonction:'energy columnist at "The Kilowatt Monitor"',texte:"We import nearly all our energy and are surprised that the price of oil calls the shots. Dependence is a choice, repeated every morning at the pump.",si:[{var:"dependanceEnergie"}]},c12:{nom:"Joséphine Aubertin",fonction:'humour columnist at "Free Figures & Letters"',texte:'The crash is here. I was promised it would not happen again, like fine weather on the day of the village fête. The government promises to "monitor the situation closely". From a distance would be wiser.'},c13:{nom:"Rodrigue Salvignac",fonction:'columnist at "The Property Review"',texte:"Housing prices are soaring and young couples are giving up. If the bubble bursts, it will not be a surprise, just a shock. We have been warning for months and nobody is listening.",si:[{var:"bulleImmo"}]},c14:{nom:"Lucile Montferrand",fonction:'digital columnist at "The Economic Thread"',texte:"The digital sector is finally pulling the economy along. Let us support it, train people for it, let it breathe. For once, the future is not to be found in an old administrative report."},c15:{nom:"Hyacinthe Dorval",fonction:'diarist at "The Illustrated Little Accountant"',texte:"The trade deficit is worsening and the currency is weakening. We buy the whole world on credit, paying with promises. All in all, it is a rather original economic model.",si:[{var:"balanceCommerciale"},{var:"changeIndice"}]}},n={evenements:e,titres:t,chroniqueurs:a};export{a as chroniqueurs,n as default,e as evenements,t as titres};
